hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1299","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, told us, Thabit told us, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a woman A black woman was praying in the mosque. She died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost her. He asked him about her after a few days, and he was told: She died. He said: “Will you excuse me?” So he came to her grave and prayed over her."
"1300","We are Abdullah bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Ziyad Al-Qatwani, we are Khaled bin Mukhlid, Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul Al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a woman was picking up rags and sticks from the mosque, so he mentioned the hadith regarding the prayer upon The grave"
